# The generated site is committed, and the generator writes LF. Without a
# forced eol, a Windows checkout rewrites templates and output to CRLF, the
# next regenerate emits CRLF, and every generated file shows a whole-file
# diff against its LF blob -- 23 phantom modifications and line-ending churn
# in the next commit. Pin LF everywhere so regenerating is a no-op on every
# platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.webp binary
